    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to total_revenue, comprising Sales and other operating revenue, Income from equity affiliates, and Other income.\n2. For total_operating_cost, standard practice for the oil & gas industry includes all costs directly tied to operations before financing and taxes. This includes: Cost of goods sold (Crude oil and product purchases), Production/Manufacturing, SG&A, Depreciation/Depletion/Impairment, Exploration, and Non-service pension costs. 'Other taxes and duties' is excluded as it is considered a non-operating tax similar to income tax, not a cost of generating revenue.\n3. 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil' is mapped to net_income.\n4. 'Income tax expense (benefit)' is mapped to taxes.\n5. 'Interest expense' is mapped to interest_expenses.\n6. The supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., components of Other income, Depreciation, Taxes) but the primary statement line items are used as the definitive source for the normalized values.\n7. Scale is 1E6 (millions) as indicated in the statement header.\n8. All values are taken directly from the primary income statement table. Parentheses in the source indicate negative numbers, but per rule 13, the values for taxes, interest_expenses, and total_operating_cost are reported as positive numbers as they reduce income.",
